  "definition_ja": "文字や式、グラフなどが、ある数量や数量の関係を示す。「x を〜の数とする」のように、文字が何を指すかを決めるときにも使う。",
  "definition_en": "To stand for a number, a quantity, or a relationship. For example, a variable can represent an unknown number, and a graph can represent a function.",
  "latex": null,
  "spoken_en": null,
  "examples": [
    {
      "en": "So what does x represent here? Right, the number of hours she worked.",
      "ja": "じゃあ、ここの x は何を表している？ そう、彼女が働いた時間だね。",
      "register": "spoken"
    },
    {
      "en": "Let a represent Maya's age now, and write an expression for her age 5 years from now.",
      "ja": "マヤの現在の年齢を a 歳として、5 年後の年齢を表す式を書け。",
